    "done_when": "A placed launch whose fake bwrap writes the missing-source refusal four seconds after launch, with no stream record, and whose child then exits, is retried and the second attempt starts; a fake launch that writes any other refusal after the same delay is not retried; a healthy fake launch whose child stays alive past the window returns from the launch within the window rather than waiting for the child to exit. The existing early-exit control, tests/test_an_early_exit_keeps_its_status.py, stays green unchanged: the startup poll still collects the exit of a child that dies inside the window. On the base commit the first fixture is recorded as a launch failure, so the test fails there. The gate log records whether the four-second delay alone reproduces the recorded failure. Gate: tests/test_a_slow_launch_retries_a_vanished_bind.py tests/test_spawn_retries_a_vanished_bind.py tests/test_an_early_exit_keeps_its_status.py tests/test_a_failed_launch_does_not_block_its_node.py. Run the gate in the foreground on the fleet allocation, with the revision, tree and command on the log's first line; ruff check and ruff format --check report nothing added on the staged paths.",
